msgid "Policy · M5Technical · T5PolicyDay 1M1M2M3Day 2M4M5M6M7TechnicalDay 1T1T2T3Day 2T4T5T6T7 Day 2 · Module 5 · fills Sheet 4 (with M4)Governance, decision rights and the legal basisWho holds each decision — and what legal basis lets the record cross a border and be shared for a child? On the canvasSheet 4 · Trust, and who decides30 minGovernance: who holds the four decisionsArchitecture authority, standards mandate, core data set custodian, trust anchor: the holder and its formal basis. UNASSIGNED is a finding. Then the legal basis and the levers you can pull.The whole canvasWord file (A3)PDF Where it meets the journeyJ1An Onesan baby is born in TaifafekiTechnicalCredential issued to a child with no national ID.PolicyLegal basis for a facility to issue a health credential to a non-citizen child (decision right: trust anchor; legal basis: consent for dependants).J2bRegistered at home, and referredTechnicalTemporary id created at a home visit, offline.PolicyWho may create a health identity for a newborn at a home visit, and on whose consent (decision right: architecture).J4.0aOne phone holds the whole family’s recordsTechnicalParent holds the child's record on a shared device.PolicyWho may hold and share a child's record; the law on dependants.J4.0bDad creates a link to share at the clinicTechnicalConsent resource recorded; 4-digit passcode; 14-day expiry.PolicyLegal basis for opening a home record abroad on consent; procurement clause for IG conformance; who sets link protection.J4.1A Taifafeki doctor sees the full historyTechnicalAuditEvent logged in Onesa on every access, including failed passcodes.PolicyThe agreement that every view abroad leaves an entry at home, and who reads it (legal basis: cross-border). Questions for the tableJ1Does your law let a facility issue a health credential to a child who is not a citizen and has no national ID?J2bWho may create a health identity for a newborn at a home visit, and on whose consent?J4.0aWho may hold and share a child’s record: either parent, a guardian, the child from what age? What does your law say about dependants?J4.0bWhat legal basis lets a record held at home be opened by a clinician abroad, on the family’s consent?J4.0bWould one clause in your procurement — conformance to the national IG — be enough for your portal to issue this link?J4.0bWho sets how a shared link is protected — the passcode, how long it lasts, who may open it: a national rule, or the family’s choice?J4.1What agreement makes every view abroad leave an entry in the home country’s log — and who reads it? Terms you will hearElectronic immunization registryClient RegistryFacility, workforce and product registriesDose number and seriesBatch numberVerifiable credentialDigital signaturePublic key infrastructureIssuer · holder · verifierHealth certificate identifierInternational Certificate of Vaccination or ProphylaxisConsentCivil registration and vital statisticsPoint-of-Service ApplicationsInteroperabilityDigital walletPersonal health recordLifelong Health RecordInternational Patient SummaryFast Healthcare Interoperability ResourcesImplementation guideProfileProcurement conditionsApplication programming interfaceGlobal Digital Health Certification NetworkTrust listHealth information exchange M5 in the journeys viewerDiscussionModule × journey mapAll modules"
